ences in performance and monoaminergic activity</article-title><source><italic>Hormones and Behavior</italic></source><year>2003</year><volume>43</volume><issue>1</issue><fpage>48</fpage><lpage>59</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12614634</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B27"><label>27</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Shors</surname><given-names>TJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Learning during stressful times</article-title><source><italic>Learning &#x00026; Memory</italic></source><year>2004</year><volume>11</volume><issue>2</issue><fpage>137</fpage><lpage>144</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15054128</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B28"><label>28</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sandi</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The role and mechanisms of action of glucocorticoid involvement in memory storage</article-title><source><italic>Neural Plasticity</italic></source><year>1998</year><volume>6</volume><issue>3</issue><fpage>41</fpage><lpage>52</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9920681</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B29"><label>29</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>M&#x000e1;rquez</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Nadal</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Armario</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Influence of reactivity to novelty and anxiety on hypothalamic-pituitary-adrenal and prolactin responses to two different novel environments in adult male rats</article-title><source><italic>Behavioural Brain Research</italic></source><year>2006</year><volume>168</volume><issue>1</issue><fpage>13</fpage><lpage>22</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16303185</pub-id></element-citation